(515616, 50166, 12475, '<td valign="top">I didn''t comment earlier--but this is one of my favorites of the challenge. I''m sad that it didn''t place higher! But excellent work. It''s original, creative, and nicely executed.</td>', 'I didn''t comment earlier--but this is one of my favorites of the challenge. I''m sad that it didn''t place higher! But excellent work. It''s original, creative, and nicely executed.', '2003-12-17 11:14:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(515626, 50304, 12475, '<td valign="top">This was one of my favorite shots of the challenge; love it.</td>', 'This was one of my favorite shots of the challenge; love it.', '2003-12-17 11:21:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(515627, 50239, 7778, '<td valign="top">To me, and apparently a handful of other voters, this image was ribbonesque. The key to appreciate the poignancy of this photo, perhaps, is to be able to discern what it is not.</td>', 'To me, and apparently a handful of other voters, this image was ribbonesque. The key to appreciate the poignancy of this photo, perhaps, is to be able to discern what it is not.', '2003-12-17 11:21:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(515634, 49483, 7364, '<td valign="top">Obviously this shot didn''t tickle the pallete of most DPC voters, that''s too bad.  I think it''a  nice photgraph and you did a good job processing.  I know this isn''t a difficult effect to achieve and should be used sparingly, but I think you picked the right time to use it.  It''s simple! :-)    My only wish is that it was bigger!  As is, it would make a terriffic postage stamp.  <br/> <br/>Anyway, nice shot, thanks for submiting  it.</td>', 'Obviously this shot didn''t tickle the pallete of most DPC voters, that''s too bad.  I think it''a  nice photgraph and you did a good job processing.  I know this isn''t a difficult effect to achieve and should be used sparingly, but I think you picked the right time to use it.  It''s simple! :-)    My only wish is that it was bigger!  As is, it would make a terriffic postage stamp.   Anyway, nice shot, thanks for submiting  it.', '2003-12-17 11:24:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(515657, 49504, 12475, '<td valign="top">Sorry I didn''t comment during the challenge; I really liked this shot and gave it one of my highest scores. The soft focus and subtle lighting worked for me, and it''s so invested with emotion. Great job.</td>', 'Sorry I didn''t comment during the challenge; I really liked this shot and gave it one of my highest scores. The soft focus and subtle lighting worked for me, and it''s so invested with emotion. Great job.', '2003-12-17 11:44:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(515711, 50259, 9763, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments.  I find it sad that I can''t submit a cat and get higher marks.  People just don''t like pet photos here I heard, no matter how good or interesting they may be.  So, I guess I know better for next time, though my cats are my life!  <br/> <br/>As for noise in the photo, that''s just his fur.  He has VERY odd fur, multi-colored strands.  There is some light reflection in his fur though.  Thank you all for taking a look at my photo.  I do appreciate it!  :)</td>', 'Thanks for your comments.  I find it sad that I can''t submit a cat and get higher marks.  People just don''t like pet photos here I heard, no matter how good or interesting they may be.  So, I guess I know better for next time, though my cats are my life!   As for noise in the photo, that''s just his fur.  He has VERY odd fur, multi-colored strands.  There is some light reflection in his fur though.  Thank you all for taking a look at my photo.  I do appreciate it!  :)', '2003-12-17 12:39:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(515717, 50152, 9411, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>Crikey!  How to comment.<br/> <br/>This was one of my 10 votes during the challenge. So needless to say I love it.<br/>The tones, shadows and textures are perfect in my estimation.<br/> <br/>Highlighting the top edge of the plate was a stroke of genius. That little extra bit of definition really pulled the shot off. Without it I think too much fade would have lessened the definition and drama.<br/> <br/>A wonderful shot.<br/> <br/>Congratulations.<br/>JC<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  Crikey!  How to comment. This was one of my 10 votes during the challenge. So needless to say I love it.The tones, shadows and textures are perfect in my estimation. Highlighting the top edge of the plate was a stroke of genius. That little extra bit of definition really pulled the shot off. Without it I think too much fade would have lessened the definition and drama. A wonderful shot. Congratulations.JC', '2003-12-17 12:49:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(515719, 49806, 9411, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the critique club</b> <br/> <br/>I think this shot could have benefited from more DOF and a little better lighting.<br/>It''s just a tad washed out.<br/> <br/>With the composition you chose, the stamen (?) [green long bit] should have been in focus as it is one of the main elements in the shot.<br/> <br/>Actually I think the entire shot should have had sharper focus to really work.<br/> <br/>A valiant effort.<br/> <br/>Of course, just my opinion.<br/> <br/>JC</td>', 'Greetings from the critique club  I think this shot could have benefited from more DOF and a little better lighting.It''s just a tad washed out. With the composition you chose, the stamen (?) [green long bit] should have been in focus as it is one of the main elements in the shot. Actually I think the entire shot should have had sharper focus to really work. A valiant effort. Of course, just my opinion. JC', '2003-12-17 12:52:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(515724, 50277, 4090, '<td valign="top">knew this would be a winner ... stunning colours . well done</td>', 'knew this would be a winner ... stunning colours . well done', '2003-12-17 12:59:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(515725, 50009, 3037, '<td valign="top">Great first shot with a digi cam. DOF could have been a little deeper, and you should see stdavidson''s walls...wow. =-)</td>', 'Great first shot with a digi cam. DOF could have been a little deeper, and you should see stdavidson''s walls...wow. =-)', '2003-12-17 12:59:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(515732, 50143, 3037, '<td valign="top">Dang those hygometer scratches. They always ruin my shots as well, but you still scored 3 10s. The real question is: why do you have a hygrometer in the middle of the Arizona?</td>', 'Dang those hygometer scratches. They always ruin my shots as well, but you still scored 3 10s. The real question is: why do you have a hygrometer in the middle of the Arizona?', '2003-12-17 13:03:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(515760, 49930, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I liked this one during the challenge because it fit it very well.  To me if it was a calm, quiet shot and relaxing it was at least a couple of points ahead of the others.  Your shot met that requirement.  <br/> <br/>I love the composition, the cropping, all very well done.  The negative space in the shot really lends to the simplicity of the shot.  What doesn''t help is the table covering.  It looks almost like a jean material?  It looks noisy and the grain the material is overall a distraction to me.  A simple black card or even white one might have offered even more simplicity to the shot.<br/> <br/>As for the clove of garlic itself, the tear in the front is also a bit of distraction.  Maybe if another side was shown so it was a smooth line?  The lighting is great and would probably work well with a black card or material and really simplify the shot to me.<br/> <br/>Again, great shot, lots of potential.<br/> <br/>Good Luck In Future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/>DNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I liked this one during the challenge because it fit it very well.  To me if it was a calm, quiet shot and relaxing it was at least a couple of points ahead of the others.  Your shot met that requirement.   I love the composition, the cropping, all very well done.  The negative space in the shot really lends to the simplicity of the shot.  What doesn''t help is the table covering.  It looks almost like a jean material?  It looks noisy and the grain the material is overall a distraction to me.  A simple black card or even white one might have offered even more simplicity to the shot. As for the clove of garlic itself, the tear in the front is also a bit of distraction.  Maybe if another side was shown so it was a smooth line?  The lighting is great and would probably work well with a black card or material and really simplify the shot to me. Again, great shot, lots of potential. Good Luck In Future Challenges! DeanndaDNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!', '2003-12-17 13:34:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(515766, 50112, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hi!  This is a great overall shot and it looks very candid, not set up at all but for this type of shot that''s very important.    <br/> <br/>Essentially you have met the challenge in offering a simple pastime as your interpitation and that works very well for me.  The absolute joy on their faces is priceless and to be treasured always.<br/> <br/>The problems with taking shots like these are trying to make sure everything is just right and this one is very close.  The brightness of the snow is a bit blinding, just like in real life and just like in real life you almost need sunglasses to look at it for any length of time.  The overall compostion of the shot is very well done.  YOu mention cropping out the trees in the background and the crop you made works very well.  The line of one foot in the lower right corner taking you through the first person into the second and their head in the upper left is very well done.  Not sure that was intentional but it works very nicely.<br/> <br/>How to improve it?  Well, not much in a shot like this unless you want to play in Photoshop and try to tone the snow down just a bit but then that takes away from the overall feel of the shot.  It''s a wonderful shot and you did very well with it.<br/> <br/>Good Luck In Future Challenges!<br/> <br/>Deannda<br/>DNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hi!  This is a great overall shot and it looks very candid, not set up at all but for this type of shot that''s very important.     Essentially you have met the challenge in offering a simple pastime as your interpitation and that works very well for me.  The absolute joy on their faces is priceless and to be treasured always. The problems with taking shots like these are trying to make sure everything is just right and this one is very close.  The brightness of the snow is a bit blinding, just like in real life and just like in real life you almost need sunglasses to look at it for any length of time.  The overall compostion of the shot is very well done.  YOu mention cropping out the trees in the background and the crop you made works very well.  The line of one foot in the lower right corner taking you through the first person into the second and their head in the upper left is very well done.  Not sure that was intentional but it works very nicely. How to improve it?  Well, not much in a shot like this unless you want to play in Photoshop and try to tone the snow down just a bit but then that takes away from the overall feel of the shot.  It''s a wonderful shot and you did very well with it. Good Luck In Future Challenges! DeanndaDNeufer@stny.rr.com if you have any questions or want to discuss this further!', '2003-12-17 13:41:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(515821, 50277, 15107, '<td valign="top">Can''t believe I missed this one when voting on the others.<br/>Definately deserves it''s top spot</td>', 'Can''t believe I missed this one when voting on the others.Definately deserves it''s top spot', '2003-12-17 14:31:45.000000', NULL, 0),
