(521144, 49622, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>Very nice definately fits the challenge well has a very simple feeling to it.  I''m not sure if it is the clouds swirl that is distracting but I feel like I am in Kansas and waiting for the twister to touch down and pick up the barn at any minute.  No matter what though it is a good photo and you did well with it.  Just think the clouds took it from simple to where you are looking for for more.</td>', 'Critique Club Very nice definately fits the challenge well has a very simple feeling to it.  I''m not sure if it is the clouds swirl that is distracting but I feel like I am in Kansas and waiting for the twister to touch down and pick up the barn at any minute.  No matter what though it is a good photo and you did well with it.  Just think the clouds took it from simple to where you are looking for for more.', '2003-12-23 15:58:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(521151, 49530, 6202, '<td valign="top">Critique Club<br/> <br/>This image is just lacking in lighting, it throws the whole thing off.  Also, you have two bullets in good focus, two slightly softer, then that first one on the left is just to far out of focus.  Something you may not have thought is the normal person reads from left to right.  Even when looking at photos the eye looks from the left to right of the photo, so of course first thing you see is that out of focus bullet and it just ruins the rest of the image.<br/> <br/>As for meeting the challenge I am the wrong person to answer that as I personally have a big dislike for anything related to guns.   I don''t believe it to meet the challenge as guns are anything but simple, however to others they would feel it meet.  I would say work on the lighting and you could get a good photo out of this.</td>', 'Critique Club This image is just lacking in lighting, it throws the whole thing off.  Also, you have two bullets in good focus, two slightly softer, then that first one on the left is just to far out of focus.  Something you may not have thought is the normal person reads from left to right.  Even when looking at photos the eye looks from the left to right of the photo, so of course first thing you see is that out of focus bullet and it just ruins the rest of the image. As for meeting the challenge I am the wrong person to answer that as I personally have a big dislike for anything related to guns.   I don''t believe it to meet the challenge as guns are anything but simple, however to others they would feel it meet.  I would say work on the lighting and you could get a good photo out of this.', '2003-12-23 16:05:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(521157, 49790, 772, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club :)<br/> <br/>Hi Kosmik...<br/> <br/>I think this is an excellent example of simplicity.  The negative space adds a great deal to that for me.  The image itself looks simplistic, but the emotion created by the image feels quite complex.  Being in the spotlight is a complex situation.  Attention to detail when in that situation is critical and complex at the same time :)  There is a feeling of desperation in this image... a sense of weariness... burden...<br/> <br/>There could have possibly been another opportunity in this photo by movign the light source out of the frame as well... I don''t think it would make any impact on the theme, but it could present a slightly different feel...<br/> <br/>Excellent work as usual :)<br/> <br/>John Setzler<br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club :) Hi Kosmik... I think this is an excellent example of simplicity.  The negative space adds a great deal to that for me.  The image itself looks simplistic, but the emotion created by the image feels quite complex.  Being in the spotlight is a complex situation.  Attention to detail when in that situation is critical and complex at the same time :)  There is a feeling of desperation in this image... a sense of weariness... burden... There could have possibly been another opportunity in this photo by movign the light source out of the frame as well... I don''t think it would make any impact on the theme, but it could present a slightly different feel... Excellent work as usual :) John Setzler', '2003-12-23 16:08:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(521408, 49840, 4482, '<td valign="top">Hmmmm.... I disapointeed with your ranking here.... I gave this a 9!!! It just sceams simplicity with an "ahhhhhhh" feeling to it. And the shalow DOF works well to keep the focus on the little lady.  :-) Great shot!! Keep it up!</td>', 'Hmmmm.... I disapointeed with your ranking here.... I gave this a 9!!! It just sceams simplicity with an "ahhhhhhh" feeling to it. And the shalow DOF works well to keep the focus on the little lady.  :-) Great shot!! Keep it up!', '2003-12-23 22:53:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(521488, 50001, 15291, '<td valign="top">Hello,<br/>     Overall I like the elements of the photo. The use of the crumbs as a leading line are a nice touch &amp; the placement of the bread is very nice. I also like the use of the color a nice blend. I also like the choice of cornbread in relation to the challage very nice. Some of the problems with the photo:. The choice of side lighting created several major problems for you here. 1) It caused what is called (blowout) loss of detail in the bread it self. 2)Rendered the front of the bread completely useless, no detail at all. 3) It created a very long distracting shadow pulling the eye away from your subject. Your leading line (entry point) into the picture is out of focus defeating the intended purpose. Most of the problems that you created with your choice of light could have been resolved by bouncing light down onto the seen. This would have given you the detail on the front &amp; side of the bread eleminated 90% of the shadow''s and given you more balance thou-out the entire photo. It would have also given you the same effect as using a warming filter which would have had a dramatic effect on the over all photo.</td>', 'Hello,     Overall I like the elements of the photo. The use of the crumbs as a leading line are a nice touch & the placement of the bread is very nice. I also like the use of the color a nice blend. I also like the choice of cornbread in relation to the challage very nice. Some of the problems with the photo:. The choice of side lighting created several major problems for you here. 1) It caused what is called (blowout) loss of detail in the bread it self. 2)Rendered the front of the bread completely useless, no detail at all. 3) It created a very long distracting shadow pulling the eye away from your subject. Your leading line (entry point) into the picture is out of focus defeating the intended purpose. Most of the problems that you created with your choice of light could have been resolved by bouncing light down onto the seen. This would have given you the detail on the front & side of the bread eleminated 90% of the shadow''s and given you more balance thou-out the entire photo. It would have also given you the same effect as using a warming filter which would have had a dramatic effect on the over all photo.', '2003-12-24 00:00:21.000000', NULL, 0),
