(537054, 50302, 14043, '<td valign="top">Yes, I forgot to sharpen it somehow, it was a last minute submit and I''d been fixing the contrast so much that I thought I did it, but I hadn''t.  *kicks self repeatedly*  Doesn''t represent anything, it''s as the title says, ''just paint.''  I have trouble getting true blacks, thus the need for Black and White, the original was, beleive it or not, brown and grainy.  That was the only way I could bring out the black background.  As for the color, well, it occured to me, but I didn''t take the time to pull some out, but it would have been lost in the B&amp;W processing anyway.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments, not that I did too well, but I felt like I had to explain some things, if just for my own silly satisfaction.<br/>~Ami~</td>', 'Yes, I forgot to sharpen it somehow, it was a last minute submit and I''d been fixing the contrast so much that I thought I did it, but I hadn''t.  *kicks self repeatedly*  Doesn''t represent anything, it''s as the title says, ''just paint.''  I have trouble getting true blacks, thus the need for Black and White, the original was, beleive it or not, brown and grainy.  That was the only way I could bring out the black background.  As for the color, well, it occured to me, but I didn''t take the time to pull some out, but it would have been lost in the B&W processing anyway. Thanks for the comments, not that I did too well, but I felt like I had to explain some things, if just for my own silly satisfaction.~Ami~', '2004-01-09 02:39:29.000000', NULL, 0),
